  "renderText": "Welcome to PvME!\nPvM Encyclopedia is a collection of resources for RuneScape combat. This channel introduces you to how our guide and text channels are organised and presented.\nGetting Involved in PvME\nIt's important to note that PvME is open source and everyone who wants to contribute is welcome. Regardless of your combat skill level, the editing team would love to have you! Check out <id:customize> and select Entry Editor\nNavigating PvME\nText channels - Interact with other PvME users in these channels.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nSocial Channels\n\nCommunity interactions, discuss the latest content, ask for help, post your achievements, and more!\n\nSocial Channels\n#general\n#osrs-general\n#other-social\n⬥ Including: Other Games, Fitness, Coding and many more!\nRS Channels\n#rs-general\n#pvm-fails\n#theorycrafting\n#achievements\nRequest Channels\n#pvm-help\n#pvm-help-forums\n#vod-reviews\n#role-submissions\n#suggestions\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n​\nThe rest of the server consists of information channels and guides.\n⬥ Use the /guides ‎command to find specific guide channels. Take note to use it in #bot-commands and NOT social channels. Other methods of searching the server include:\n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• The Ctrl + K Discord function.\n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• #directory which lists all channels currently maintained in PvME.\n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• If you've exhausted all the other options, ask in #pvm-help for help.\n​\nPVM Help\nLink: #pvm-help / #pvm-help-forums\n​\nAsk all questions related to PVM or combat in these channels frequented by @Helpers. They will likely know the answers to your questions or direct you to the relevant guide.\n​\nSome tips on channel usage:\n​\n⬥ Ask quick questions #pvm-help. When there's an ongoing conversation which may bury your question, try using a thread or post it in #pvm-help-forums.\n⬥ Make a forum post in #pvm-help-forums for complex questions requiring large amounts of information, e.g. preset help, understanding fundamentals of a style or boss.\n​\nTo help with commonly asked questions, we introduced commands. These should be used in the #bot-commands channel to provide some quick information on a variety of topics. A list of commands can be found in #command-info.\n​\nVOD Review\nLink: #vod-reviews\n​\n#vod-reviews allows you to submit recordings of your PVM encounters for others to review and give constructive, personalised, and judgement-free feedback. It is a great way to improve your PVM.\n​\nTo make a forum post in #vod-reviews:\n⬥ Name it appropriately, e.g. \"<Boss> (<Style>) - RSN\".\n⬥ Include relevant background information and/or questions.\n⬥ Include a link to your video recording.\n​\nBossing Path\nLink: #bossing-path\n​\nThe PvME bossing path provides an avenue to progress your skills and reach higher-tier PvM goals. It helps set objectives based on learning stages to measure your progression. It's perfect if you're new to bossing and unsure of where to start or looking for objectives to facilitate advancing your current abilities.\n​\nThe Mastery System\nLink: #unknown-channel / #unknown-channel\n​\nThe PvME Mastery System is a great way to gauge your PvM progress. It provides meaningful goals to shoot for as you learn new content or hone your skills at familiar encounters. There are multiple tiers of mastery ranks, each one granting its own unique role colour for all to see.\n​\nPvME Boss Guides\nThe focus of our community is providing the best text guides possible for every encounter and players of all skill levels. Described below is the general composition of our guides. Each guide contains a table of contents at the bottom, with links to help you navigate the guide quickly.\n​\nHeader/Banner\nEach guide contains a header or \"banner\" image, containing a few key pieces of information for each encounter. An example is show below for Osseous, the Rex Matriarch:\n\nIn order of circles shown in the above example:\n​\n\n\nNumbers represent the boss' size (for example 5x5 tiles)\n\n\n indicates whether the SGB special attack can be used\n\n\n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Note: it is recommended to not use   on a boss with size 1x1 or 2x2\n\n\n indicates whether the boss is poisonable or not\n\n\n indicates whether a familiar will be able to do damage to the boss\n\n\nSlayer perks ( undead,  demon and  dragon) indicate a boss' weakness\n\n\n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Note: when added as Invention perks to your gear, these will increase damage dealt to the boss by 7% and generally do not stack\n​\nSuggested Presets\n⬥ PvME provides one or more suggested preset(s) in every strategy guide.\n⬥ Historically, presets were presented as images with a link to a full breakdown of the items used.\n⬥ Since the creation of https://pvme.github.io/preset-maker/, PvME is in the process of converting presets to a more condensed format, complete with familiars, relics, and more.\n⬥ Examples of both formats can be found below.\n​\n⬥ Presets usually DO NOT need to be strictly copied.\n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Downgrading a little bit is usually fine.\n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• If a boss guide that has strict gear requirements that must be adhered to, it will be clearly stated.\n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• If unsure, ask questions relating to presets and their contents in #pvm-help.\n⬥ Presets in full boss guides generally assume best in slot perks listed in #perks\n⬥ Presets in basic and AFK boss guides generally assume basic perks listed in #perks\n⬥ Downgrading your preset from the recommended may mean that rotations will need some extra improvisation.\nPreset format example (Ranged HM Vorkath)\nPresets and Relics\n⬥ Ranged \n\n⬥ On task, prefer blue dragon / dragon cluster tasks to undead, which is depleted by minion kills\n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Highest task count is blue dragons\n⬥  and  used\n⬥  and  for sustain\n⬥ T100  \n⬥ Use  on Vorkath and  on Zemouregal\n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Use  as needed\n⬥ The following are not needed:   / phyical  /  /  / \n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Can use  \n​\nMechanics & Suggested Ability Rotations\n⬥ Following basic information and preset suggestions, guides will generally mention:\n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Specific boss mechanics.\n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• DPS ability rotations.\n​\nThe rotations listed in full boss guides are designed for optimal kills!\nSome considerations to take when following these are:\n​\n⬥ Abilities used to deal with specific mechanics should be adhered to strictly.\n⬥ Most DPS rotations are generally only suggestions and need not be followed exactly\n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Feel free to adapt them as you see fit!\n⬥ Due to RNG you may need to improvise these rotations based on damage dealt, adrenaline etc.\n​\nMany of our guides make use of abbreviations. Check them out in this document: https://runescape.wiki/w/Glossary.\n​\n      \n    ",
